<title>USA: Meredith CEO backs EPS consensus.</title>
<headline>Meredith CEO backs EPS consensus.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Meredith Corp supports analysts' consensus view that it will earn $0.60 a share for the second quarter ending December 31 and $2.35 for the full fiscal year 1997, Chief Executive Officer William Kerr told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;They are clearly in line with the consensus view and certainly met our expectations,&quot; Kerr said in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>The Des Moines-based publishing and television company will report quarterly results next Tuesday.</p>
<p>Meredith was trading at 52-3/8, up 5/8.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
